 "verdict_detail": {
  "headline": "The whole second-order load of p2 is one singular component (i=8, s=1.481e-21, amplitude +82.81) of the prolonged matrix. Removing it would erase the load (|L_J| reduction 94.40, >> floor_J2 = 3.241; Shat00^(2) would go from -162.648 to -6.3e-8) but the prolonged row residual rises from 6.44e-21 to 1.00e-19, ten times the registered 1e-20 bar. Every other removal or truncation that cuts the load by more than floor_J2 likewise breaks the residual bar (truncations at P=3: residual 1.00e-19; at P=4: 8.61e-19; the P=4 untruncated solve: 9.56e-20). The PRICE RE-READ trigger is therefore NOT met at any swept setting (its residual condition fails everywhere), and P133-2's price stands as computed, now with its irreducibility in the registered basis stated.",
  "price_reread_triggered": false,
  "kappa2_moves": false,
  "second_path_discrepancy": "Reported, not averaged: the load-carrying direction sits at s8 = 1.481e-21, BELOW the inter-engine assembly difference ||M_bachfloat - M_bachgen||_F = 2.40e-20. On the bachfloat assembly s8 = 7.80e-21 (factor 5.3), its L_J share is 4.52 (vs 94.40), the total L_J[p2] is (-1.577, +0.00049, -3.286, +2.674) and Shat00^(2) = -1.275, and |v8_prim . v8_sec| = 0.553. The DECIDING features agree on both paths: exactly one near-null component carries ~100% of the load (all others <= 1.1e-7), its removal breaks the 1e-20 residual bar on both (1.00e-19 primary; 1.32e-20 second), the well-conditioned spectrum s0..s7 agrees to <= 1.6e-11 relative, and kappa^(2) = 0 on both."
